# Skullcrack: "Players can't gain life this turn. Damage can't be prevented this turn. Skullcrack deals 3 damage to target
# player or planeswalker." Bot2's Kor Firewalker (protection from red) blocks Bot1's red Embereth Shieldbreaker. In the
# declare blockers step Bot1 casts Skullcrack at Bot2. The Firewalker's "whenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1
# life" goes on the stack above it and resolves first (its ruling), so Bot2 still gains the 1 (21). Then Skullcrack resolves:
# Bot2 takes 3 (18), and protection's prevention can't apply to the Shieldbreaker's combat damage this turn (CR 615.12,
# 702.16e): the Firewalker is dealt 2 and dies, as does the Shieldbreaker. Nothing is prevented.

